+## Context
+
+Each defect is local to one function; see proposal.md. Money helpers already provide `percentOf`, which rounds half up and is used for shipping VAT.
+
+## Decisions
+
+- `Catalog.find` normalises with the existing `canonicalSku` (trim + upper-case), the same function `add` uses, so lookup and storage cannot diverge. Alternative of lower-casing at call sites rejected: it would leave other entry points broken.
+- `shippingCost` uses `>=` against the threshold; the constant is already €50.00.
+- `lineVat` delegates to `percentOf` rather than a new rounding routine, matching `shippingVat`.
+
+## Risks / Trade-offs
+
+- Inventory is keyed by exact SKU strings and `Inventory.restock` does not normalise; orders always pass the canonical SKU, so the reported bug is unaffected. Normalising inventory is out of scope.
