@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+## Why
+
+Three reports show the code departing from the README business rules: a lower-case SKU is refused as unknown, an order of exactly €50.00 pays shipping, and line VAT is rounded down instead of half up.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- SKU lookup in the catalogue trims surrounding spaces and ignores case, so `lb-220` finds `LB-220` (today it only trims, so only the upper-case form matches).
+- Shipping is free when goods after every discount, before VAT, are €50.00 **or more** (today only strictly above €50.00).
+- Line VAT is rounded half up to the cent (today it is truncated: €1.99 at 22% gives 0.43 instead of 0.44).
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `product-catalog`: SKU identity and lookup rules.
+- `shipping`: shipping cost and the free-shipping threshold.
+- `vat`: VAT rates and rounding on lines.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+## Impact
+
+- `src/catalog.ts` (`find`), `src/shipping.ts` (`shippingCost`), `src/tax.ts` (`lineVat`); tests in `test/`.
+- Orders already placed are unaffected; invoices and receipts follow the corrected amounts for new orders.
